        "Attributes": [
          {
            "Id": 758309,
            "attributeType": "LongString",
            "attributeName": "AIDescription",
            "attributeRelationType": "None",
            "Value": "The Game Boy Color, released in 1998, was Nintendo's evolution of the classic Game Boy, bringing vibrant color to a beloved handheld. Powered by a custom Nintendo CPU CGB and a Sharp SM83 processor (capable of dual-speed mode), it offered enhanced performance and four times the memory of its predecessor. The device featured a 2.3-inch TFT LCD screen displaying a 160x144 pixel resolution, and was backward compatible with original Game Boy titles. \n\nDevelopers were encouraged to create enhanced versions of existing games, often labeled \"Deluxe\" or \"DX,\" like *Tetris DX* and *The Legend of Zelda: Link's Awakening DX*. Popular titles like *Pokémon Gold and Silver* cemented its success, with over 23 million units sold. While short-lived, succeeded by the Game Boy Advance, the Game Boy Color sold 118.69 million units worldwide, solidifying its place in gaming history."
          },
